# `then` sequencing (Example 10): <action> then <body>.
# The action evaluates to a duration; `then` waits that long, then runs
# the body. Only valid in a state on-entry body (like `wait`).

function telegraph():
    print("telegraph")
    return 0.2s

scene Demo:
    initial: go

    state go:
        print("enter go")
        telegraph() then
            print("strike")
        0.1s then
            print("after pause")
        -> done

    state done:
        print("enter done")
